  "notes": "Modified cash basis, so basis=cash. All funds governmental (nutrition program is within Other Governmental Funds); no business-type funds. Basic statement from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Fund Balances Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5). Loan proceeds greater than 12 months (36,500) recorded as debt_proceeds and included in printed total receipts. Transfers (net) are 94,064 into General and (94,064) out of Other Governmental Funds, net zero in total column, so top-level transfers null. Ending cash is the balance sheet total assets/cash 3,410,412 (p6); the roll-forward statement prints ending fund balance 3,410,413 (fund columns 2,247,692+824,847+337,873 = 3,410,412), a 1 dollar printing difference. Beginning cash = beginning fund balance 2,060,393 (p5). General Fund detail uses the General Fund Components combining schedule Total column (General + Depreciation funds, eliminations applied) rather than the more itemized General Fund budget schedule (p11-14), which excludes the Depreciation Fund and includes transfers; not recorded to avoid double counting. Other fund schedules added: School Nutrition (p16), Qualified Capital Purpose Undertaking (p17), Special Building (p18), Activities (p19). Transfers on those schedules (QCP out 100,000; Activities in 5,936) recorded as other financing, signed; the Activities transfer of 5,936 is also printed as General Fund 8000 Transfers on p14 (due to activity fund). Qualified Capital Purpose schedule prints transfers out as its only disbursement line, so no expenditure total recorded for it; Activities schedule prints no total receipts, so no revenue total recorded. Student transportation 247,772 on p9 is after the (200,000) Depreciation Fund transfer elimination (flagged). Basic statement Other 3,248 is a mix of licenses, carline tax, corporate grants, fines and nutrition rebates; recorded as licenses and permits with review. Fix pass (attempt 3): General Fund Components p8 revenue lines add to the printed Total receipts 8,010,324 (which includes Loan Proceeds 36,500 but NOT the Transfers - net 94,064, printed on p9 below Total disbursements). The 94,064 was previously added to the revenue check through the 'includes other financing' rule, causing the +94,064 mismatch; no line was double counted or misread. The transfer line is kept as other financing under a distinct fund label so it is not added into the revenue total. Read pages 1-19 of 19 of the trimmed PDF (pages 11-19 hold the budget schedules recorded earlier). Audit3 fix: Support services - Students split by its p4 fund columns (General 417,035 support services; Other Governmental Funds 368,402 student activities = Activities Fund disbursements p19).",
